Subject: [PATCH 08865/11362] ARC P1-P6 results; fix artifact-freshness gate
 blocking on inherited staleness

Operator directive 2026-08-11: "do all of the plans: P1-P6, unattended", then
"fix blockage".

THE GATE FIX. artifact-freshness-lint refused a commit for staleness the
committer neither caused nor touched. The conductor commits with --no-verify by
design, so it changes shared agent modules without ever running the hook and
dependent artifacts silently rot; by today twelve had, several drifting on their
OWN analyser or build scripts, so rebuilding them would legitimately move
published numbers. The next person to touch any trigger file inherited a refusal
they could not clear -- which trains people toward --no-verify, the exact failure
this module's docstring says it exists to prevent.

drift_is_pre_existing() now re-checks each drifted dependency against HEAD. An
artifact blocks only when a drifted dependency MATCHED its recorded hash at HEAD
(fresh before, broken now). When all drift predates HEAD it is reported as
BACKLOG with a count and does not block. Verified both directions: 12 backlog
artifacts exit 0, and dirtying one dependency of a fresh artifact still exits 1
with "REFUSING THE COMMIT". _sha256_at_head returns None on any git failure and
the caller keeps blocking -- fail-closed, stated in the docstring.

Two pre-existing test failures are deliberately NOT fixed: both assert every
registered artifact is fresh and both fail on the backlog. Confirmed they fail
identically using HEAD's own check_artifact, which this change does not touch.
They correctly report the debt and must not be relaxed to pass.

RESULTS.
P1 exp6250 -- prospective ensemble A/B: selector matched the held-optimal arm 3
of 3; pooled held-out 0.5118 beat BOTH pure arms (linear 0.2032, rex 0.4810). The
gate failed on COVERAGE only: sc25 produced no candidate from either arm, and the
gate required all four roster games. tu93 is the case the mechanism exists for --
linear returned a worthless engine (0.0), rex an excellent one (0.9259), same
budget, and the VALID score alone identified it.

P2 exp6251 -- best-of-N: NO reliable gain. One win (cn04), one loss (g50t), and
two games with no headroom (0.0 floor, 1.0 ceiling), so the pooled improvement is
cn04 alone -- the same one-outlier shape exp6248 was retired for, and my gate was
too permissive to catch it. g50t is the important row: the selector picked a
candidate whose VALID more than doubled while its HELD fell, so the VALID proxy
that went 9-for-9 in P1 missed one of only two real decisions here. Recorded as a
tension, not a refutation. min_distinct_sources=4 proves a genuine N=4.

P3 exp6252 -- RETRACTED and re-run; see the earlier entries. Corrected result is
a clean negative. The real finding is that collect_transitions destroys win
states, so the goal-aware question cannot be asked offline at all.

P4 -- config knobs shipped, defaults byte-identical; the argv test caught a
latent UnboundLocalError that would have broken every live generator launch.
P5 -- kernel preview A/B built, 0 deletions, scored path byte-identical, NOT
pushed to Kaggle.
P6 exp6254 -- re-running after I found a store-path bug in my own script that
made every arm return no candidate.

